# oracle: pair lj/cut/dipole/long 2.5 + kspace_style pppm/dipole 1.0e-4 with the automatic G-ewald and mesh (accuracy 1.0e-4), 108 fcc point dipoles (dipole/random, |mu| 0.7) in a periodic box, run 0: pe, elong, press and the per-atom forces and torques
# oracle-files: w135pd_auto_fcc_tq.dump
# measured with native LAMMPS (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, b332f28): the automatic G-ewald is 1.3859120 (native, printed 1.385912) and 1.3859114 (engine); the relative difference 4e-7 is the one Newton step of adjust_gewald, whose finite-difference derivative (h = 1e-6) follows the last digits of the k-space error. The engine agrees with native at fixed G (kspace_modify gewald 1.3769898 mesh 32 32 32: the printed estimated accuracy agrees to 8 digits). Error at the automatic G: thermo ecoul 3.2e-6 relative, forces 1.7e-7, torques 2.4e-8 under Node 24; under Node 20 2.3e-6, 1.2e-7, 1.7e-8. The compare tolerance is set to those values, not to 1e-8.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=5e-6 atomrel=5e-7 filerel=5e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 0.4
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
set             group all diameter 1.0
set             group all density 1.0
set             group all dipole/random 4421 0.7
pair_style      lj/cut/dipole/long 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dipole 1.0e-4
# automatic G-ewald and mesh (no kspace_modify)
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
run             0
write_dump      all custom w135pd_auto_fcc_tq.dump id tqx tqy tqz modify format float %.15g sort id
